---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { loadContent } from "../../lib/content";
import { calBookingUrl } from "../../lib/site";

const { provider } = loadContent();
---

<Layout
  title={`Coordinate Geometry | CBSE Class 10 Maths | ${provider.name}`}
  description="CBSE Class 10 Maths Chapter 7 study notes on Coordinate Geometry. Distance formula, collinearity, section formula (internal division), midpoint formula, centroid of triangle, and an interactive 20-question board exam quiz."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="small" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/subjects/">Subjects</a> / <a href="/resources/">Resources</a> / Coordinate Geometry
    </nav>

    <div class="resource-header">
      <span class="eyebrow">CBSE Class 10 · Mathematics · Chapter 7</span>
      <h1>Coordinate Geometry</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Connect algebra and geometry on the Cartesian plane. Master the Distance Formula, Section Formula (m₁ : m₂), Mid-point Formula, and geometric classification of shapes for the CBSE Class 10 Board Exam.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Core Concepts -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Key Concepts &amp; Formulas</h2>

      <div class="grid two concept-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>📏 The Distance Formula</h3>
          <p class="formula">d = √[(x₂ - x₁)² + (y₂ - y₁)²]</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li><strong>Distance between points P(x₁, y₁) and Q(x₂, y₂):</strong> Derived directly from Pythagoras theorem on the Cartesian plane.</li>
            <li><strong>Distance from Origin (0, 0):</strong> <code>OP = √(x² + y²)</code>.</li>
            <li>Distance is always a non-negative scalar quantity (<code>d ≥ 0</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Collinearity:</strong> Three points A, B, and C are collinear if <code>AB + BC = AC</code> (the sum of lengths of two segments equals the third).</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>✂️ The Section Formula (Internal Division)</h3>
          <p class="formula">P(x, y) = [(m₁x₂ + m₂x₁)/(m₁ + m₂), (m₁y₂ + m₂y₁)/(m₁ + m₂)]</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li>Coordinates of point <em>P(x, y)</em> which divides the line segment joining <em>A(x₁, y₁)</em> and <em>B(x₂, y₂)</em> internally in ratio <code>m₁ : m₂</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Ratio trick (k : 1):</strong> When finding the unknown ratio in which a point or axis divides a line, assume the ratio is <code>k : 1</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Division by X-axis:</strong> The y-coordinate of the dividing point is <strong>0</strong> (<code>y = 0</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Division by Y-axis:</strong> The x-coordinate of the dividing point is <strong>0</strong> (<code>x = 0</code>).</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>📍 Mid-Point &amp; Centroid Formulas</h3>
          <p class="formula">Mid-point: [(x₁ + x₂)/2, (y₁ + y₂)/2]</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li><strong>Mid-point of AB:</strong> Special case of Section Formula when <code>m₁ : m₂ = 1 : 1</code>.
              <br/><code>M = ((x₁ + x₂)/2, (y₁ + y₂)/2)</code>.
            </li>
            <li><strong>Centroid of Triangle ABC:</strong> Intersection of medians, dividing each median in ratio <code>2 : 1</code> from vertex:
              <br/><code>G = ((x₁ + x₂ + x₃)/3, (y₁ + y₂ + y₃)/3)</code>.
            </li>
            <li><strong>Parallelogram 4th vertex property:</strong> Diagonals of a parallelogram bisect each other (their mid-points are identical).</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>🔷 Identifying Geometric Quadrilaterals &amp; Triangles</h3>
          <p class="formula">Using distance conditions</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li><strong>Equilateral Triangle:</strong> All 3 sides equal (<code>AB = BC = CA</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Isosceles Triangle:</strong> Any 2 sides equal.</li>
            <li><strong>Right Triangle:</strong> Satisfies Pythagoras theorem: <code>AB² + BC² = AC²</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Square:</strong> 4 sides equal AND both diagonals equal (<code>AB=BC=CD=DA</code> and <code>AC=BD</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Rhombus:</strong> 4 sides equal BUT diagonals are unequal (<code>AC ≠ BD</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Rectangle:</strong> Opposite sides equal AND diagonals equal.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Visual Diagrams Section -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Visual Concepts: Distance Triangle &amp; Section Ratio Division</h2>

      <div class="grid two">
        <div class="card visual-card">
          <div class="visual-badge">Visual Diagram 1 · Pythagorean Distance Construction</div>
          <div class="svg-container">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 460 250" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Distance formula as hypotenuse of right triangle">
              <rect width="460" height="250" fill="#f8fafc" rx="8"/>
              
              <!-- Axes -->
              <line x1="40" y1="210" x2="420" y2="210" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2"/>
              <line x1="60" y1="30" x2="60" y2="230" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2"/>
              <text x="425" y="214" font-size="11" fill="#64748b">X</text>
              <text x="60" y="24" font-size="11" fill="#64748b" text-anchor="middle">Y</text>

              <!-- Points P and Q -->
              <!-- P(120, 150) -> x1, y1 -->
              <!-- Q(340, 60) -> x2, y2 -->
              <!-- R(340, 150) -> right angle -->
              <polygon points="120,150 340,150 340,60" fill="#e0f2fe" stroke="#bae6fd" stroke-width="1"/>
              
              <!-- Hypotenuse PQ -->
              <line x1="120" y1="150" x2="340" y2="60" stroke="#0f766e" stroke-width="3"/>
              
              <!-- Base PR -->
              <line x1="120" y1="150" x2="340" y2="150" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="2"/>
              <!-- Altitude RQ -->
              <line x1="340" y1="150" x2="340" y2="60" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="2"/>

              <!-- Right angle symbol at R -->
              <rect x="325" y="135" width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="1.5"/>

              <!-- Point markers -->
              <circle cx="120" cy="150" r="5" fill="#0f766e"/>
              <text x="105" y="165" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#0f766e">P(x₁, y₁)</text>

              <circle cx="340" cy="60" r="5" fill="#0f766e"/>
              <text x="355" y="60" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#0f766e">Q(x₂, y₂)</text>

              <!-- Dimension labels -->
              <text x="230" y="170" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="600" fill="#0284c7">Base = |x₂ - x₁|</text>
              <text x="385" y="110" font-size="11" font-weight="600" fill="#dc2626">Height = |y₂ - y₁|</text>
              <text x="210" y="95" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#0f766e">d = √[(Δx)² + (Δy)²]</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <p class="visual-caption">Distance formula derived from Pythagoras theorem: Hypotenuse² = (Base)² + (Height)².</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card visual-card">
          <div class="visual-badge">Visual Diagram 2 · Section Formula (Internal Division m₁ : m₂)</div>
          <div class="svg-container">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 460 250" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Section formula internal division">
              <rect width="460" height="250" fill="#f8fafc" rx="8"/>
              
              <!-- Line AB -->
              <line x1="60" y1="130" x2="400" y2="130" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="3"/>

              <!-- Point A -->
              <circle cx="60" cy="130" r="6" fill="#0284c7"/>
              <text x="60" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#0284c7">A(x₁, y₁)</text>

              <!-- Point B -->
              <circle cx="400" cy="130" r="6" fill="#0284c7"/>
              <text x="400" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#0284c7">B(x₂, y₂)</text>

              <!-- Dividing Point P -->
              <circle cx="196" cy="130" r="6" fill="#ef4444"/>
              <text x="196" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#dc2626">P(x, y)</text>

              <!-- Ratio bracket m1 -->
              <path d="M 65 145 Q 128 170 190 145" fill="none" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="2"/>
              <text x="128" y="180" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#0284c7">Ratio m₁</text>

              <!-- Ratio bracket m2 -->
              <path d="M 202 145 Q 298 175 395 145" fill="none" stroke="#ea580c" stroke-width="2"/>
              <text x="298" y="185" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#ea580c">Ratio m₂</text>

              <!-- Cross multiplication schema box -->
              <rect x="70" y="200" width="320" height="36" rx="6" fill="#ecfdf5" stroke="#10b981"/>
              <text x="230" y="222" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#065f46">x = (m₁x₂ + m₂x₁)/(m₁ + m₂), &nbsp; y = (m₁y₂ + m₂y₁)/(m₁ + m₂)</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <p class="visual-caption">Internal division of a line segment with cross-ratio weighting: m₁ multiplies B's coordinates and m₂ multiplies A's.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Solved Step-by-Step Problem -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Exemplar Board Problem: Ratio by X-Axis &amp; Point of Division</h2>
      <div class="card" style="padding:1.75rem; background:var(--paper)">
        <h3 style="color:var(--brand);margin-top:0">Problem: Find the ratio in which the line segment joining the points A(1, -5) and B(-4, 5) is divided by the X-axis. Also find the coordinates of the point of division.</h3>
        <div style="font-size:0.95rem; line-height:1.7; color:var(--text)">
          <p><strong>Step 1 (Formulate division point):</strong> Any point on the X-axis has its y-coordinate equal to zero.
            <br/>Let the point of division on the X-axis be <code>P(x, 0)</code>, and let the required ratio be <code>k : 1</code>.
          </p>
          <p><strong>Step 2 (Apply section formula for y):</strong>
            <br/>Here <code>y₁ = -5, y₂ = 5, m₁ = k, m₂ = 1</code>.
            <br/><code>y = (m₁y₂ + m₂y₁) / (m₁ + m₂)</code>
            <br/><code>0 = [k(5) + 1(-5)] / (k + 1)</code>
            <br/><code>0 = 5k - 5 &nbsp;⟹&nbsp; 5k = 5 &nbsp;⟹&nbsp; k = 1</code>.
            <br/>Therefore, the ratio is <code>1 : 1</code> (meaning P is the <strong>mid-point</strong> of AB!).
          </p>
          <p><strong>Step 3 (Find x-coordinate):</strong>
            <br/>Using <code>k = 1</code>:
            <br/><code>x = (m₁x₂ + m₂x₁) / (m₁ + m₂) = [1(-4) + 1(1)] / (1 + 1) = (-4 + 1) / 2 = -3/2</code>.
          </p>
          <p><strong>Conclusion:</strong>
            <br/>The ratio is <strong>1 : 1</strong>, and the coordinates of the point of division are <strong>(-3/2, 0)</strong>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Interactive 20-Question Quiz -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Interactive CBSE Board Exam Quiz (20 Questions)</h2>
      <p class="muted">Test your command over distance formulas, section ratio calculations, midpoints, and geometric shapes on the coordinate grid.</p>

      <div class="quiz-container card" id="quiz-box">
        <div class="quiz-header-bar">
          <span class="quiz-counter" id="quiz-counter">Question 1 of 20</span>
          <span class="quiz-score" id="quiz-score">Score: 0 / 20</span>
        </div>

        <div class="quiz-question-body">
          <p class="quiz-q-text" id="quiz-question">Loading question...</p>
          <div class="quiz-options-list" id="quiz-options"></div>
          <div class="quiz-feedback" id="quiz-feedback"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="quiz-footer-actions">
          <button class="button secondary" id="quiz-prev-btn" disabled>← Previous</button>
          <button class="button" id="quiz-next-btn" disabled>Next Question →</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="quiz-completed-banner card" id="quiz-result-box" style="display:none; text-align:center; padding:2.5rem;">
        <h3>Quiz Completed! 🎉</h3>
        <p class="quiz-final-score" id="quiz-final-score" style="font-size:1.4rem; font-weight:700; color:var(--brand); margin:1rem 0;"></p>
        <p id="quiz-final-msg" class="muted"></p>
        <button class="button" id="quiz-restart-btn" style="margin-top:1rem;">Retake Quiz</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="cta-banner">
      <h2>Need personalized Maths guidance for Class 10?</h2>
      <p>Book a free {provider.trial.duration_minutes}-minute trial session with {provider.tutor_name} (online or at-home) to master coordinate geometry, section formulas, and full marks board presentation.</p>
      <a class="button" href={calBookingUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book Free Trial</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
(function() {
  const quizData = [
    {
      q: "The distance of the point P(-6, 8) from the origin is:",
      options: ["8", "2√7", "10", "6"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "Distance from origin = √(x² + y²) = √[(-6)² + 8²] = √(36 + 64) = √100 = 10 units."
    },
    {
      q: "The distance between the points A(0, 6) and B(0, -2) is:",
      options: ["6", "8", "4", "2"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Since x-coordinates are both 0, distance is |y₂ - y₁| = |-2 - 6| = |-8| = 8 units."
    },
    {
      q: "If the distance between the points (4, p) and (1, 0) is 5, then the value of p is:",
      options: ["4 only", "±4", "-4 only", "0"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "d² = (4 - 1)² + (p - 0)² = 5² ⟹ 3² + p² = 25 ⟹ 9 + p² = 25 ⟹ p² = 16 ⟹ p = ±4."
    },
    {
      q: "The coordinates of the mid-point of the line segment joining the points (-5, 4) and (7, -8) are:",
      options: ["(1, -2)", "(-1, 2)", "(1, 2)", "(-1, -2)"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "Mid-point = [(-5 + 7)/2, (4 + (-8))/2] = [2/2, -4/2] = (1, -2)."
    },
    {
      q: "If P(a/3, 4) is the mid-point of the line segment joining Q(-6, 5) and R(-2, 3), then the value of a is:",
      options: ["-4", "-12", "12", "-6"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "x-coordinate of mid-point = (-6 + (-2))/2 = -8/2 = -4. Given a/3 = -4 ⟹ a = -12."
    },
    {
      q: "The point which divides the line segment joining (7, -6) and (3, 4) in the ratio 1 : 2 internally lies in the quadrant:",
      options: ["I", "II", "III", "IV"],
      answer: 3,
      explanation: "x = [1(3) + 2(7)]/(1 + 2) = (3 + 14)/3 = 17/3 > 0. y = [1(4) + 2(-6)]/3 = (4 - 12)/3 = -8/3 < 0. Point (+, -) lies in Quadrant IV."
    },
    {
      q: "The perimeter of a triangle with vertices (0, 4), (0, 0), and (3, 0) is:",
      options: ["5", "12", "11", "7 + √5"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Sides are: Distance (0,0) to (0,4) = 4; (0,0) to (3,0) = 3; (0,4) to (3,0) = √(3² + 4²) = 5. Perimeter = 4 + 3 + 5 = 12 units."
    },
    {
      q: "The ratio in which the Y-axis divides the line segment joining the points (5, -6) and (-1, -4) is:",
      options: ["1 : 5", "5 : 1", "2 : 3", "3 : 2"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "On Y-axis, x = 0. Let ratio be k : 1. x = [k(-1) + 1(5)]/(k + 1) = 0 ⟹ -k + 5 = 0 ⟹ k = 5. Ratio is 5 : 1."
    },
    {
      q: "If A(1, 3), B(-1, 2), C(2, 5), and D(x, 4) are the vertices of a parallelogram ABCD, then the value of x is:",
      options: ["3", "4", "0", "5"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "In parallelogram, mid-point of diagonal AC = mid-point of diagonal BD. (1 + 2)/2 = (-1 + x)/2 ⟹ 3 = x - 1 ⟹ x = 4."
    },
    {
      q: "The point P on the X-axis which is equidistant from the points A(2, -5) and B(-2, 9) is:",
      options: ["(0, -7)", "(-7, 0)", "(7, 0)", "(0, 7)"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Let P(x, 0). PA² = PB² ⟹ (x - 2)² + (0 - (-5))² = (x - (-2))² + (0 - 9)² ⟹ x² - 4x + 4 + 25 = x² + 4x + 4 + 81 ⟹ -4x + 29 = 4x + 85 ⟹ 8x = -56 ⟹ x = -7. Point is (-7, 0)."
    },
    {
      q: "If three points A(0, 0), B(3, √3), and C(3, λ) form an equilateral triangle, then λ is:",
      options: ["2", "-3", "-√3", "0"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "Distance AB = √(3² + 3) = √12. AC² = 3² + λ² = 9 + λ² = 12 ⟹ λ² = 3 ⟹ λ = ±√3. For C distinct from B, λ = -√3."
    },
    {
      q: "The coordinates of the centroid of a triangle whose vertices are (0, 6), (8, 12), and (8, 0) are:",
      options: ["(16/3, 6)", "(8, 6)", "(6, 6)", "(16, 18)"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "G = [(0 + 8 + 8)/3, (6 + 12 + 0)/3] = (16/3, 18/3) = (16/3, 6)."
    },
    {
      q: "The line segment joining points (-3, -4) and (1, -2) is divided by Y-axis in ratio:",
      options: ["1 : 3", "2 : 3", "3 : 1", "3 : 2"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "On Y-axis, x = 0. Ratio k : 1 gives x = [k(1) + 1(-3)]/(k + 1) = 0 ⟹ k - 3 = 0 ⟹ k = 3. Ratio is 3 : 1."
    },
    {
      q: "Which point lies on the perpendicular bisector of the segment joining (-2, -5) and (2, 5)?",
      options: ["(0, 0)", "(0, 2)", "(2, 0)", "(-2, 0)"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "The mid-point is [(-2 + 2)/2, (-5 + 5)/2] = (0, 0). The perpendicular bisector passes through the midpoint (0, 0)."
    },
    {
      q: "The distance of point P(3, 4) from the X-axis is:",
      options: ["3 units", "4 units", "5 units", "1 unit"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "The perpendicular distance of any point (x, y) from the X-axis is |y| = |4| = 4 units."
    },
    {
      q: "If points A(k, 2k), B(3k, 3k), and C(3, 1) are collinear, then k is:",
      options: ["-1/3", "1/3", "-1", "2"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "Slope AB = slope BC. (3k - 2k)/(3k - k) = (1 - 3k)/(3 - 3k) ⟹ k/(2k) = 1/2. 1/2 = (1 - 3k)/(3 - 3k) ⟹ 3 - 3k = 2 - 6k ⟹ 3k = -1 ⟹ k = -1/3."
    },
    {
      q: "The center of a circle is (2a - 1, 7) and it passes through (-3, -1). If the diameter is 20 units, then the value of a is:",
      options: ["-4 or 2", "4 or -2", "-4 or -2", "4 or 2"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Radius = 20 / 2 = 10 units. Radius² = (2a - 1 - (-3))² + (7 - (-1))² = 10² ⟹ (2a + 2)² + 8² = 100 ⟹ (2a + 2)² + 64 = 100 ⟹ (2a + 2)² = 36 ⟹ 2a + 2 = ±6. If 2a + 2 = 6 ⟹ 2a = 4 ⟹ a = 2. If 2a + 2 = -6 ⟹ 2a = -8 ⟹ a = -4. Wait, let's check signs: a = 2 or -4 (option A or B). When a = -4, 2(-4)+2 = -6, (-6)²=36. When a = 2, 2(2)+2 = 6, 6²=36. So a = -4 or 2."
    },
    {
      q: "If the points (1, 2), (0, 0), and (a, b) are collinear, then:",
      options: ["a = b", "a = 2b", "2a = b", "a = -b"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "Since (0, 0) is one point, the line is y = mx. Using (1, 2), m = 2/1 = 2. Thus the equation is y = 2x. Since (a, b) lies on it, b = 2a."
    },
    {
      q: "The vertices of a triangle are (4, 4), (3, -2), and (-3, 16). The area of the triangle is:",
      options: ["30 sq units", "27 sq units", "0 sq units (Collinear)", "15 sq units"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Area = 1/2 |4(-2 - 16) + 3(16 - 4) + (-3)(4 - (-2))| = 1/2 |4(-18) + 3(12) + (-3)(6)| = 1/2 |-72 + 36 - 18| = 1/2 |-54| = 27 sq units."
    },
    {
      q: "Points P(2, 3), Q(4, 0), and R(6, -3) are:",
      options: ["Vertices of a right triangle", "Collinear points", "Vertices of an equilateral triangle", "None of these"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Slope PQ = (0 - 3)/(4 - 2) = -3/2. Slope QR = (-3 - 0)/(6 - 4) = -3/2. Since slopes are equal and Q is a common point, P, Q, and R are collinear."
    }
  ];

  // Fix answer index for question 17: -4 or 2 is option 0
  quizData[16].answer = 0;

  let currentIdx = 0;
  let userAnswers = new Array(quizData.length).fill(null);

  const qText = document.getElementById("quiz-question");
  const optionsBox = document.getElementById("quiz-options");
  const feedbackBox = document.getElementById("quiz-feedback");
  const counterBox = document.getElementById("quiz-counter");
  const scoreBox = document.getElementById("quiz-score");
  const prevBtn = document.getElementById("quiz-prev-btn");
  const nextBtn = document.getElementById("quiz-next-btn");
  const quizBox = document.getElementById("quiz-box");
  const resultBox = document.getElementById("quiz-result-box");
  const finalScore = document.getElementById("quiz-final-score");
  const finalMsg = document.getElementById("quiz-final-msg");
  const restartBtn = document.getElementById("quiz-restart-btn");

  function renderQuestion(idx) {
    const item = quizData[idx];
    counterBox.textContent = `Question ${idx + 1} of ${quizData.length}`;
    qText.textContent = item.q;
    optionsBox.innerHTML = "";
    feedbackBox.textContent = "";
    feedbackBox.className = "quiz-feedback";

    const selected = userAnswers[idx];

    item.options.forEach((optText, oIdx) => {
      const btn = document.createElement("button");
      btn.className = "quiz-opt-btn";
      btn.textContent = `${String.fromCharCode(65 + oIdx)}. ${optText}`;

      if (selected !== null) {
        btn.disabled = true;
        if (oIdx === item.answer) {
          btn.classList.add("opt-correct");
        } else if (oIdx === selected) {
          btn.classList.add("opt-wrong");
        }
      } else {
        btn.onclick = () => selectOption(oIdx);
      }

      optionsBox.appendChild(btn);
    });

    if (selected !== null) {
      if (selected === item.answer) {
        feedbackBox.textContent = `✓ Correct! ${item.explanation}`;
        feedbackBox.classList.add("feedback-correct");
      } else {
        feedbackBox.textContent = `✗ Incorrect. Correct answer is option ${String.fromCharCode(65 + item.answer)}. ${item.explanation}`;
        feedbackBox.classList.add("feedback-wrong");
      }
    }

    prevBtn.disabled = idx === 0;
    nextBtn.disabled = selected === null;
    nextBtn.textContent = idx === quizData.length - 1 ? "Finish Quiz →" : "Next Question →";
    updateScoreDisplay();
  }

  function selectOption(oIdx) {
    userAnswers[currentIdx] = oIdx;
    renderQuestion(currentIdx);
  }

  function updateScoreDisplay() {
    let score = 0;
    userAnswers.forEach((ans, i) => {
      if (ans === quizData[i].answer) score++;
    });
    scoreBox.textContent = `Score: ${score} / ${quizData.length}`;
  }

  prevBtn.onclick = () => {
    if (currentIdx > 0) {
      currentIdx--;
      renderQuestion(currentIdx);
    }
  };

  nextBtn.onclick = () => {
    if (currentIdx < quizData.length - 1) {
      currentIdx++;
      renderQuestion(currentIdx);
    } else {
      finishQuiz();
    }
  };

  function finishQuiz() {
    quizBox.style.display = "none";
    resultBox.style.display = "block";
    let score = 0;
    userAnswers.forEach((ans, i) => {
      if (ans === quizData[i].answer) score++;
    });
    finalScore.textContent = `Your Final Score: ${score} / ${quizData.length} (${Math.round((score / quizData.length) * 100)}%)`;
    if (score >= 18) {
      finalMsg.textContent = "Outstanding mastery! You have complete command over coordinate formulas, ratios, and geometric validations.";
    } else if (score >= 14) {
      finalMsg.textContent = "Great job! Review collinearity conditions and the k : 1 section ratio technique to reach perfection.";
    } else {
      finalMsg.textContent = "Keep revising! Review the formulas and exemplar problem above, then re-attempt the quiz.";
    }
  }

  restartBtn.onclick = () => {
    userAnswers = new Array(quizData.length).fill(null);
    currentIdx = 0;
    resultBox.style.display = "none";
    quizBox.style.display = "block";
    renderQuestion(0);
  };

  renderQuestion(0);
})();
</script>

